<node id="1193698" title="Re: Escaping double quotes in complete document" created="2017-06-27 10:32:17" updated="2017-06-27 10:32:17" _doctext_mode="lenient"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="241598">holli</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">This is the minimal code to use a templating engine named Template::Toolkit. 
&lt;code&gt;
my $tt = Template-&gt;new();

$tt-&gt;process( \q[&lt;html&gt;
  &lt;!--Foo--&gt;
  &lt;input type="text" name="mytext" id="mytext" value="[% soap_result %]"/&gt;
  &lt;!--Bar--&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;], { soap_result =&gt; $soap_result }) || die $tt-&gt;error(), "\n";
&lt;/code&gt;
This protects you from Cross-Site-Scripting attacks and handles the double quote issue.
